PS4 game-audio capture for the ProsperoSunshine port.

PBS's PS4 backend captures video only (it sets audio to "none"). libSceAvcap also
exports sceVshAvcapOpenAudioEx / sceVshAvcapReadAudio (confirmed on fw 14.00), and the
audio handle is Started like the video handle. Disassembly of libSceAvcap shows ReadAudio
is mechanically identical to ReadVideo (same nonblocking ring read), so the existing
worker export-reader serves audio verbatim once pointed at ReadAudio.

RemotePlay uses OpenAudioEx (not the plain OpenAudio): the two stubs differ only in one
byte passed to the shared open worker (OpenAudio=1, OpenAudioEx=0). ps4debug on a live
Remote Play session (SceRemotePlay pid 47) located remoteplay's own call site
OpenAudioEx(&handle, &obj+0x204) and read the exact 16-byte config it passes:
  [0x00]=0  [0x04]=0  [0x08]=1  [0x0C]=0x1f400 (128000)
+0x04 is 0, so the libSceAvcap config[+4]==2 branch (extra shared-handle setup, needing
caller cooperation we never provided — the cause of the earlier 0x80a90005) is skipped;
this is the normal full game-audio session. The caller supplies those bytes (see
ps_pbs_audio_open in pbs_session.c).

This adds, all inside the authorized SceRemotePlay worker context:
  - export_reader: a symbol variant so a reader can bind sceVshAvcapReadAudio.
  - remote.c: pbs_ps4_remote_audio_open/read/close (OpenAudioEx with a caller-supplied
    config, its own Start, exported ReadAudio, Stop/Close).
  - capture.c/.h: pbs_ps4_audio_open/read/close dispatching to the remote backend.

